sion is a policy (\"/v2 for public routes, /v1 frozen\"), not something tied to particular files. `invalidated_by` only takes paths or globs, so I set it to `src/api/`. That makes the memory flag \"revisit if src/api/ changes\", which fires on any edit there, not on a real change to the versioning policy. I would have liked a free-text or event-style invalidation trigger, such as \"when a /v3 is announced or the freeze is lifted\".\n- **Duplicate check:** I ran one filter query on \"API versioning v1 v2 routes\". It returned only the unrelated problem+json convention, with a low score. I judged that to mean no existing versioning memory, but the result gave no clear \"no relevant match\" signal. A relevance cutoff or an explicit empty result would have made that call easier.\n- **Scope:** I wasn't sure whether a decision about public API routes should go in the project store or a shared one. I used the project store, since nothing indicated related repos. A scope hint in the create response would have helped."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 12564, "cache_read_input_tokens": 10131, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 12564}, "output_tokens": 6, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [{"type": "thinking_dropped", "path": "messages.2.content.0", "reason": "prefix_binding_mismatch"}], "diagnostics": {"cache_miss_reason": {"type": "tools_changed", "cache_missed_input_tokens": 21248}}, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f4c4847a-3a97-47f6-8518-752f46f1e64f", "uuid": "5c9b3da8-a623-4cb0-836b-658f189ce7c1", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T13:21:07.185Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbaxsH4tsrPwQ3DK9i8B"}, {"type": "rate_limit_event", "rate_limit_info": {"status": "allowed", "resetsAt": 1790865000, "rateLimitType": "five_hour", "overageStatus":